    narr:narration """This position holds that output caps should not bound ordinary output: as [Scarlet's evaluation argues](narr:Expr_20261011_1_VerifyPr1031WrappingQuotesRepairOnDev_h2e601120d6cc_34), a cap belongs only on runaway behavior — [the circuit-breaker framing](narr:Expr_20261011_1_VerifyPr1031WrappingQuotesRepairOnDev_h2e601120d6cc_34) — with length requests left to the prompt. The stance moved from argument to [codification as a rule](narr:Expr_20261011_1_VerifyPr1031WrappingQuotesRepairOnDev_h2e601120d6cc_35) the same day.""" ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_20261011_1_VerifyPr1031WrappingQuotesRepairOnDev_h2e601120d6cc_34> ;
